ent release that was healthy in production, in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the service in a mixed state; the retry completed the rollout to all regions. Post-rollback status: v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. v2.3.1 remains unhealthy in production and should not be redeployed until it is fixed. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial-failure.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2-2025"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent production release that was healthy. v2.3.1 was unhealthy in all regions. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the regions mixed. The retry completed the rollout.\n- **Current state:** v2.3.0 is running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. The service reports healthy, with error rate down from 0.18 to 0.002.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback, and the partial-failure retry. The first incident request timed out, so I retried it with the same idempotency key. That key ensures only one incident was opened.\n\nv2.3.1 should not be redeployed until its failure is understood. The orchestrator partial failure also needs follow-up.", "type": "text"}]}]}